SUMMARY:Humans in the Loop: Building and hiring for AI at Questrade
DESCRIPTION:TechTO\n​This is a free event\, but approval is required. Pl
 ease apply through this link: https://luma.com/humans-in-the-loop-nov-19-2
 026\n\n**AI agents are becoming the new front door to financial products\,
  and most companies don’t own that interface. So how do you build someth
 ing people can trust anyway?**\n\n​Join us for an evening with Questrade
 ’s engineering\, product\, and hiring leaders. You’ll hear candid talk
 s and a presentation on what it takes to ship real software in the era of 
 Agentic AI\, including how we built a production MCP server enabling custo
 mers to use their own AI tools\, with a human deterministically in the loo
 p.\n\n**Why attend**\n\n* ​**See how we built it:** why we created an MC
 P server\, and how granular authorization keeps customers in control.\n* 
 ​**Go deep on the hard parts:** authentication and delegation for agents
  acting on a customer’s behalf\, and how we design the experience when a
 n agent sits between us and our customers.\n* ​**Learn how we measure it
 :** tool evals\, performance at scale\, and how we bring users up the trus
 t ladder.\n* ​**Meet the humans behind it:** Questrade’s engineering\,
  product\, and AI leaders\, plus the hiring managers and team members you
 ’d work with. Hear how we hire for AI and ask them anything about the wo
 rk and the teams building it.\n\n​We’ll close the night with an open n
 etworking reception\, so you can keep the conversation going over drinks a
 nd passed canapés.\n\n**Agenda**\n\n* ​**5:30 pm:** Doors open. Check i
 n and mingle.\n* ​**6:30 pm:** Talk and live demo: *Humans in the Loop: 
 Building and hiring for AI at Questrade* (presented by Bartek Kowalski\, P
 roduct Manager\, MCP\, and Kelvin Ferreira\, Senior Principal Software Eng
 ineer)\n* ​**7:00 pm:** Panel and open Q&A with Questrade’s engineerin
 g\, product\, and hiring leaders\n* ​**7:30 pm:** Networking reception w
 ith open bar and passed canapés\n* ​**9:00 pm:** End of evening\n\n**Wh
 o it's for**\n​Engineers\, product managers\, and AI professionals who w
 ant a real look at how a Canadian fintech builds and hires in this space.\
 n\n**On stage**\n\n* **​[Kelvin Ferreira](https://www.linkedin.com/in/ke
 lvinrodri/?utm_source=luma)\, Senior Principal Software Engineer:** Kelvin
  is a hands-on engineer behind Questrade’s MCP and API strategy. He desi
 gns how AI agents connect to Questrade securely – from OAuth 2.1 authent
 ication and delegation to granular\, tool-level permissions – making sur
 e customers stay in control of every action.\n* **​[Bartek Kowalski](htt
 ps://www.linkedin.com/in/bartek-kowalski-68117b1ab/?utm_source=luma)\, Pro
 duct Manager\, MCP:** Bartek leads product for Questrade’s MCP\, shaping
  how customers experience Questrade through the AI tools they already use.
  He works on a hard question: how do you build trust and a great product w
 hen you don’t own the interface?\n* **​[Andrej Simeonov](https://www.l
 inkedin.com/in/drej/?utm_source=luma)\, Head of Technology\, Questrade Exp
 erience Platform:** Andrej leads the engineering behind the Questrade Expe
 rience Platform\, the foundation that powers how millions of Canadians int
 eract with their money. He’s focused on building infrastructure that sca
 les reliably while staying ready for new ways of reaching customers\, incl
 uding AI agents.\n* **​[David Wieler](https://www.linkedin.com/in/davidw
 ieler/?utm_source=luma)\, Chief AI Officer:** David shapes the architectur
 e and AI infrastructure strategy across the Questrade ecosystem. He leads 
 how the company adopts AI and agentic tooling safely and at scale\, from t
 he platforms engineers build on to the standards that keep them secure.\n\
 n![User Uploaded Image](https://images.lumacdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=au
 to\,fit=cover\,dpr=2\,quality=75\,width=800\,height=233.84615384615384/upl
 oads/8v/81c91c66-ad89-44c7-b60f-633b3ab5bac3.png)**Open roles at Questrade
